  "id": "running-wheel",
  "term": "running wheel",
  "definition": "A running wheel is a motor-driven exercise wheel used in animal research to measure and support sustained running, in this case in rats. In the described infrared-sensing version, sensors track the animal’s position in real time so researchers can record and quantify effective exercise activity objectively.",
